id: pm-xe0c38
title: "Holistic pm CLI, SDK, and ecosystem optimization roadmap"
description: "Manual whole-system review and deduplicated delivery map for the pm CLI, public SDK, repository architecture, multi-agent storage semantics, agent UX, performance, security, and official external package fleet."
type: Plan
status: open
priority: 0
tags[6]: audit,changelog-exclude,context-management,ecosystem,planning,roadmap
created_at: "2026-07-24T12:06:36.504Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-24T12:09:37.874Z"
assignee: claude-code-agent
author: claude-code-agent
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "All current pm items and official packages are evaluated from live state; every finding is mapped to a canonical owner or a duplicate-checked focused item; measured regressions include reproducible evidence and fixed non-weakenable budgets; plan captures sequencing across CLI, SDK, architecture, performance, security, multi-agent safety, and packages; no implementation code or generated changelog is changed; tracker integrity passes; tracker-only commit is pushed directly to main."
goal: project management = context management
objective: "A deduplicated, evidence-backed roadmap makes pm simpler, faster, safer, more extensible, and easier for agents without feature loss."
value: Future agents can resume from live canonical owners instead of repeating broad review work or creating overlapping backlog.
why_now: "The command surface, SDK, tracker corpus, and official package fleet have all changed materially; current performance and ecosystem-quality evidence must be reconciled before further implementation."
parent: pm-doxj
risk: medium
confidence: high
