plan_decisions[2]{ts,author,decision,rationale,evidence}:
  "2026-07-24T12:07:20.356Z",claude-code-agent,Reuse living capability epics and focused owners instead of creating a replacement audit umbrella.,"Live all-status search and full metadata show complete canonical coverage for CLI simplification, SDK completeness, quality, architecture, scale, merge safety, security, and dependency policy.","pm-doxj, pm-n7rr, pm-usfg, pm-92if, pm-9rxu, pm-ugqx, pm-quzx and their current children."
  "2026-07-24T12:07:21.012Z",claude-code-agent,Keep the scale failure and external fleet conformance gap as separate focused work.,One is a reproducible current-main regression against fixed host budgets; the other is a cross-repository governance capability. Bundling would obscure acceptance and ownership.,pm-hcrmye and pm-feecbs.
plan_discoveries[3]{ts,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T12:07:21.786Z",claude-code-agent,"The core repository has exact 100% all-source coverage and zero configured code clones, yet four infrastructure files are above 99% of the effective-LOC cap and the widest source directory contains 70 direct files."
  "2026-07-24T12:07:22.445Z",claude-code-agent,"Every official published external package passed isolated runtime smoke, but no external repository exposes lint or coverage scripts and shared or vendored source duplication remains material."
  "2026-07-24T12:07:23.082Z",claude-code-agent,"Agent-facing recovery is generally actionable: unsupported search and create flags returned exact ownership hints. Nested positional-action help and read-only init status mutation remain owned by existing help/init lineages."
