body: "This plan records the current whole-system review under the philosophy project management = context management. Core behavior is unusually well protected: literal all-source coverage, zero local code clones, public SDK boundary enforcement, contract generation, token budgets, security scans, isolated package dogfood, and merge-aware git storage. The most important delivery principle is simplification without capability loss: consolidate presentation grammar, decompose implementation modules and folders, and single-source package policy while retaining every typed SDK primitive, compatibility alias, storage invariant, and history record.\n\nRecommended delivery order:\n- Restore the fixed 10k latency and RSS budgets through pm-hcrmye; continue pm-801d and the scale program after the regression is understood.\n- Execute the accepted noun-verb grammar and tiered-discovery sequence under pm-n7rr, preserving hidden aliases and contract parity.\n- Decompose saturated files through pm-yh8r and reorganize high-fan-out domain folders through pm-kb5h while keeping public SDK exports stable.\n- Retain pm-usfg as the functional SDK completeness contract; use pm-f4yn, pm-j8vq, and the quality/security lineages for maintainability and analyzer debt.\n- Establish pm-feecbs under the trust ladder, then apply pm-quzx dependency and canonical-package decisions across all official packages.\n- Prioritize open mutation races pm-khdq and pm-zwib plus fresh-init/merge-fence issues before claiming conflict-free multi-agent operation at fleet scale.\n- Preserve authoritative TOON item documents, append-only attributable history, semantic merge drivers, strict reconciliation, bounded context outputs, and SDK-first implementation in every tranche.\n\nNo product source, test, documentation, dependency, workflow, threshold, or release asset is changed by this plan."
